-- rules/inquiry/epistemic.rofl — epistemic states as a derived ledger.
-- [epistemic] is the book of conclusions of this discipline; these four
-- rules are its only writers (docs/choosing-perspectives.md).
--
-- Invariants carried here (roadmap §20):
--   Absence of evidence must not derive falsehood: `refuted` needs an
--   explicit refutes[obs] entry; no evidence at all yields `unknown`.
--   `contested` keeps both sides visible instead of collapsing them.

-- stale evidence supports and refutes nothing; staleness is defined by
-- rules/policies/evidence.rofl (undefined => nothing is ever stale).
-- Evidence may target an alias; it counts for the canonical claim
-- (rules/inquiry/terminology.rofl; identity when no mapping exists).
supported[epistemic](C) :- claim(C), supports[obs](E, T), canonical(T, C),
                           not stale_evidence[epistemic](E).
refuted[epistemic](C)   :- claim(C), refutes[obs](E, T), canonical(T, C),
                           not stale_evidence[epistemic](E).

contested[epistemic](C) :- supported[epistemic](C), refuted[epistemic](C).

unknown[epistemic](C)   :- claim(C),
                           not supported[epistemic](C),
                           not refuted[epistemic](C).

-- Confirmation grades (decision b, 2026-08-28): a polarity link attached by
-- an AGENT (visible as agent_basis) reaches the confirmed grade only after
-- an explicit confirmed_polarity(E, C) fact — asserted by a human or a
-- runtime tool run (authority-gating of the confirmer can follow the
-- accepted_gap pattern later). Links the runtime entered natively (no
-- agent_basis anywhere) are confirmed by construction. Blocking verdicts
-- (obligations.rofl) use ONLY the confirmed grade; non-blocking obligations
-- live on the plain grade — the asymmetry is the point.

agent_attached[main](E, C)        :- agent_basis[P](T, E), canonical(T, C).

pending_polarity(C, E)            :- agent_attached(E, C),
                                     not confirmed_polarity(E, C).

supported_confirmed[epistemic](C) :- claim(C), supports[obs](E, T),
                                     canonical(T, C),
                                     not stale_evidence[epistemic](E),
                                     not agent_attached(E, C).
supported_confirmed[epistemic](C) :- claim(C), supports[obs](E, T),
                                     canonical(T, C),
                                     not stale_evidence[epistemic](E),
                                     confirmed_polarity(E, C).

refuted_confirmed[epistemic](C)   :- claim(C), refutes[obs](E, T),
                                     canonical(T, C),
                                     not stale_evidence[epistemic](E),
                                     not agent_attached(E, C).
refuted_confirmed[epistemic](C)   :- claim(C), refutes[obs](E, T),
                                     canonical(T, C),
                                     not stale_evidence[epistemic](E),
                                     confirmed_polarity(E, C).
